{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"encoder-motor","name":"Gear motor with encoder","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"The yellow TT gear motor with a 20-slot encoder disc and an optical sensor on its shaft: its OUT pin changes as the slots pass, so a board can count how far and how fast it turned. Drive it like any TT motor (through a motor driver).","category":"Motion","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// A TT gear motor (driven by the volts across M+ and M-) with a slotted disc on its shaft. The\n// optical sensor's OUT is high while a slot lets its light through: 20 slots, 40 changes a turn.\nbench.device('tt-encoder', (part) => {\n  const shaft = part.motor('shaft');\n  let volts = 0, encV = 0, out = 0, edges = 0;\n  // average volts on a pin (PWM counts by its duty)\n  const avg = (io, pin) => {\n    const v = io.v(pin) ?? 0, p = io.pwm(pin);\n    return p ? v * p.duty : v;\n  };\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      volts = avg(io, 'M+') - avg(io, 'M-');\n      if (Math.abs(volts) < 0.3) shaft.power(0, 6);\n      else shaft.power(Math.sign(volts), Math.abs(volts));\n      // the encoder\n      encV = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      const slot = ((Math.floor(shaft.angle / 9) % 2) + 2) % 2;\n      if (slot !== out) { out = slot; edges++; }\n      if (encV >= 2.8) io.drive('OUT', out ? encV : 0, 1);\n      else io.release('OUT');\n      io.draw((encV >= 2.8 ? 0.01 : 0) + Math.min(1, Math.abs(volts) / 6) * 0.15 + (Math.abs(volts) > 0.3 && Math.abs(shaft.speed) < 10 ? 0.5 : 0));\n    },\n    status() {\n      const rpm = Math.round(shaft.speed / 6);\n      return [`${volts.toFixed(1)} V, ${rpm} rpm`, encV >= 2.8 ? `encoder ${edges} changes` : 'encoder: no power (VCC)'];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","parts":[{"id":"tt-encoder","name":"TT motor + encoder (20 slots)","description":"M+ and M- to a motor driver (3-6 V, about 200 rpm at 6 V, 0.8 kg*cm). The encoder: VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, OUT changes level each time a slot edge passes: 40 changes a turn (20 rising edges). Glue a wheel to its shaft.","swatch":"#f2c230","mass":32,"shape":[{"box":[6.4,2.2,1.9],"at":[0,1.1,0],"color":"#f2c230"},{"cyl":[1,2.6],"at":[4.1,1.1,0],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#c9cdd4"},{"box":[1.4,0.16,2],"at":[-1.6,1.1,-1.6],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#1d4fb8"},{"box":[0.5,0.6,0.5],"at":[-1.6,1.8,-1.35],"color":"#141416"}],"pins":[{"id":"M+","label":"Motor +","at":[5.4,1.55,0],"kind":"motor"},{"id":"M-","label":"Motor -","at":[5.4,0.65,0],"kind":"motor"},{"id":"VCC","label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","at":[-2.1,0.35,-2.4],"kind":"vin","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"GND","at":[-1.6,0.35,-2.4],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"OUT","label":"OUT (encoder)","at":[-1.1,0.35,-2.4],"kind":"out"}],"moving":[{"id":"shaft","mass":4,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.3,1],"at":[-1.6,1.1,-0.6],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"cyl":[0.95,0.08],"at":[-1.6,1.1,-1.05],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#141416"},{"cyl":[0.3,1],"at":[-1.6,1.1,1.45],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#f2f2f2"}],"joint":{"type":"turn","at":[-1.6,1.1,0],"axis":[0,0,1],"motor":"motor","torque":0.8,"speed":200,"volts":6}}],"device":"tt-encoder"}],"examples":[{"name":"Measure the speed","description":"A board drives the motor through a DRV8833 at three speeds and counts the encoder's pulses: rpm in the serial monitor.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Measure the speed","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-8,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"drv","type":"drv8833","name":"Motor driver","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,6],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"motor","type":"encoder-motor/tt-encoder","name":"Motor","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[8,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"bat","type":"battery-4aa","name":"Motor battery","params":{"count":"4","cells":"nimh","charge":100},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,14],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP6"},"b":{"uid":"drv","pin":"AIN1"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP7"},"b":{"uid":"drv","pin":"AIN2"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"drv","pin":"AOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motor","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"drv","pin":"AOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motor","pin":"M-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"bat","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"drv","pin":"VM"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"bat","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"drv","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"drv","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"motor","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"motor","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"motor","pin":"OUT"},"color":"#3fbf7f"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Count the encoder's pulses (an interrupt on each rising edge) and work out the rpm,\n// at three speeds. 20 slots on the disc: 20 pulses a turn.\n#define ENC 2\n#define AIN1 6\n#define AIN2 7\n\nvolatile long pulses = 0;\n\nvoid onPulse() {\n  pulses++;\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(AIN1, OUTPUT);\n  pinMode(AIN2, OUTPUT);\n  pinMode(ENC, INPUT);\n  attachInterrupt(digitalPinToInterrupt(ENC), onPulse, RISING);\n}\n\nvoid runAt(int power) {\n  analogWrite(AIN1, power);   // PWM: how much of the battery's volts the motor gets\n  digitalWrite(AIN2, LOW);\n  delay(500);                 // let it get up to speed\n  pulses = 0;\n  delay(1000);\n  long n = pulses;\n  Serial.print(\"power \");\n  Serial.print(power);\n  Serial.print(\": \");\n  Serial.print(n * 60 / 20);\n  Serial.println(\" rpm\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  runAt(120);\n  runAt(190);\n  runAt(255);\n  digitalWrite(AIN1, LOW);\n  Serial.println(\"stop\");\n  delay(1500);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}